        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Well appearing, ambulant, with mild guarding of the right knee; mobilising independently and in no acute distress."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-10",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-10",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right knee examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Mild fullness at the medial joint line; no deformity or erythema. Tender over the medial joint line and along the MCL; no increased warmth. Full extension with slight reduction in terminal flexion due to pain; no mechanical block. Varus and valgus stress cause medial discomfort without gross laxity. Anterior drawer grossly normal. McMurray causes medial discomfort without a definite painful click. Slightly antalgic gait favouring the right side; able to fully weight bear. No features noted to suggest acute septic arthritis or fracture."
      }
    },
